  "description": "Native DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (MXFP4 experts, FP8 dense) across four DGX Sparks with SGLang TP4/EP2 over RoCE, tuned from knapcio's TP4 profile @a544a0f1 (canary-roce image, b12x RoCEnante all-reduce on both rails, Engram prefetch) plus adaptive DSpark verify (compact ragged verify, SPS cost table, 6-file patch in the evidence): DSpark block 5, vision, 1,048,576 context, 6,000,000-token KV pool, 48 requests, 4096-token prefill chunks, --prefill-decode-interval 4, no server-side output cap (DSV41_MAX_NEW_TOKENS=0). sparkDash protocol at one request: 109.5 tok/s code, 121.2 structured, 59.0 prose. Local Inference Lab protocol: 49.2 tok/s at one request, 350.8 aggregate at 48; cold prefill about 3.4k tok/s from 8k to 128k; a cold 420k prompt completes (2.1k tok/s) and a 15.7-minute mixed stress ran with zero failures. KV pool is 6M rather than 8M so a deep cold prefill keeps >= 4.5 GB MemAvailable per node. Two of the four test Sparks ran driver 580.159.03 at ~2190 MHz vs ~2520 MHz on the others.",
